{"strongs": "H3866", "word": "לוּד", "translit": "lu.di", "root": "לוד", "morph": "N:N--LG", "pos": "proper name, masculine and of a people", "gloss": "Lud, Lydia", "definition": "לוּד , לוּדִים proper name, masculine and of a people 1. Lud, Lydia , Assyrian Luddu : — אַרְפַּכְשַׁד וְלוּד וַאֲרָם Gen 10:22 = 1Chr 1:17 ᵐ5 Λουδ . 2. apparently a people in northeast Africa תַּרְשִׁישׁ פּוּל וְלוּד Isa 66:19 , ᵐ5 Λουδ ; ׳ וּפוּט פָּרַס וְל Ezek 27:10 כּוּשׁ וּפוּט וְלוּד Ezek 30:5 ( + לוּב q. v.), in both ᵐ5 Λ ( ο ) υδοι ; also plural לוּדִים a 'son' of Misraim, Gen 10:13 ᵐ5 Λυδιειμ (|| לְהָבִים ) = 1Chr 1:11 (לוּדִי֯יםׅ ; Jer 46:9 (|| פּוּט , כּוּשׁ ) see לוּב above — On this African לוּד see Di Gen 10:13 , opposed to Sta Javan 5 ff. compare WMM As.Eur.115 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4349')\">BDB4349</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3865')\">H3865</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H3866')\">H3866</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4348')\">BDB4348</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4350')\">BDB4350</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>לוּד</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>לוּדִים</bdbheb> <b>proper name, masculine and of a people</b> <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlightword>Lud, Lydia</highlightword>, Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>Luddu</highlight></transliteration>: — <bdbheb>אַרְפַּכְשַׁד וְלוּד וַאֲרָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 10:22\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(1,10,22)\">Gen 10:22</ref> = <ref ref=\"1Chr 1:17\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(13,1,17)\">1Chr 1:17</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Λουδ</grk>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> apparently a people in northeast Africa <bdbheb>תַּרְשִׁישׁ פּוּל וְלוּד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 66:19\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"66\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"66\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(23,66,19)\">Isa 66:19</ref>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Λουδ</grk>; <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>וּפוּט פָּרַס וְל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 27:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,27,10)\">Ezek 27:10</ref> <bdbheb>כּוּשׁ וּפוּט וְלוּד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 30:5\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(26,30,5)\">Ezek 30:5</ref> ( + <bdbheb>לוּב</bdbheb> q. v.), in both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Λ</grk>(<grk>ο</grk>)<grk>υδοι</grk>; also plural <bdbheb>לוּדִים</bdbheb> a 'son' of Misraim, <ref ref=\"Gen 10:13\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(1,10,13)\">Gen 10:13</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Λυδιειμ</grk> (|| <bdbheb>לְהָבִים</bdbheb>) = <ref ref=\"1Chr 1:11\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(13,1,11)\">1Chr 1:11</ref> <bdbheb>(לוּדִי֯יםׅ</bdbheb>; <ref ref=\"Jer 46:9\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(24,46,9)\">Jer 46:9</ref> (|| <bdbheb>פּוּט</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>כּוּשׁ</bdbheb>) see  <bdbheb><reflink>לוּב</reflink></bdbheb> above — On this African <bdbheb>לוּד</bdbheb> see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di<sup><ref ref=\"Gen 10:13\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(1,10,13)\">Gen 10:13</ref>, opposed to</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sta')\">Sta<sup>Javan 5 ff.</sup></lookup> compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('WMM')\">WMM<sup>As.Eur.115</sup></lookup>. </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Gen 10:22", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 10, "verse": 22}, {"raw": "1Chr 1:17", "book": "1CH", "chapter": 1, "verse": 17}, {"raw": "Isa 66:19", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 66, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "Ezek 27:10", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 27, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Ezek 30:5", "book": "EZK", "c